The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
struct rtw_chip_info {
    ...
    u32 ch_param[3]; // part of const struct
    ...
};
```
Reason:
The `ch_param` array was part of the `const` `struct rtw_chip_info`, which means it was intended to be immutable. The 8821c implementation attempted to modify this field, leading to an illegal memory access and a core dump.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
struct rtw_chip_info {
    ...
    // Move ch_param to a mutable struct
    ...
};
```
Reason:
By moving the `ch_param` array to a different structure that is not marked as `const`, it allows the 8821c implementation to modify the channel parameters without causing illegal memory access, thus preventing the core dump.

